 ### `frai eval`
-Generate evaluation reports for model outputs.
+Generate evaluation reports for model outputs. Optionally gate the CI pipeline on threshold checks.
 - `--outputs <file>` *(required)* – JSON file with model outputs.
 - `--references <file>` – JSON file with reference answers.
 - `--report <path>` – output location (`frai-eval-report.json` by default).
 - `--format <json|markdown>` – output format (defaults to JSON). Markdown reports include human-readable summaries for review boards.
+- `--threshold <metric>=<min>` – set a minimum score for a metric (can be given multiple times). Valid metric IDs: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`. Values must be between 0 and 1. Exit code 1 if any threshold fails, 2 for usage errors, 0 if all pass (or no thresholds given).
+
+**Example:**
+```bash
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95 --format markdown
+```
+The report will include a "Thresholds" section with PASS/FAIL status for each. Metrics with no score (e.g., exact match without references) are treated as failures.
 
