+- Threshold support (`--threshold <metric>=<min>`) to gate CI pipelines on metric scores.
 
 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Thresholds
+- CLI: `--threshold <metric>=<min>` (can be given multiple times) gates the exit code on metric scores.
+  - Exit 0 if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds given).
+  - Exit 1 if any threshold fails.
+  - Exit 2 if a threshold is malformed or metric ID is unknown.
+- Core: `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object (`{ exact_match: 0.9 }`).
+  - Report gains top-level `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array with per-threshold `{ metric, min, score, passed }`.
+  - Metrics with null score (e.g., exact match without references) fail their threshold instead of crashing.
+  - Works for custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`.
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL for each.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
